{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"529f33b2cd0c3bba00d180e7f9fc58f2002be135d269d7bd51cf3e1e4ca0ca4c","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_23b3a2f069b0abacb90152c61938229234ce74ad2925f15403b6ecbbf3c92eba","overall_assessment":"The paper is well-organized with a logical flow from theoretical foundations to empirical validation. The writing is generally clear, and the notation is consistent, though the presentation of the main theorem's bound could be more precise. The figure captions are detailed and effectively describe the visual content, aiding the reader's understanding of the results.","paper_id":"B1TTpYKgx","paper_identity_sha256":"3a6379e0de312c4240e839ca99f09d13c5d6760466ea612a46799a8e1b0d3d5b","prompt_identity_sha256":"de9c4be5a064816a489c1c198ee2efd3c6433350f5c0e80c31730b35def35418","raw_response_sha256":"635344269ef0d5f7590a240f32d2044d9e043367db3cc96bac9d61ce252e788f","request_identity_sha256":"befe15cfc81dc8a911a5a3d18af51141ce8f2c6e077e2034e4cdd20b1b4c0057","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"22a4924da1c2f5c40ef296ee9f996ea15acd88cb097cbc207fb9bd0920e5a163","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-002","SRC-003","SRC-004","SRC-005","SRC-006","SRC-007","SRC-008","SRC-009","SRC-010","SRC-011","SRC-012","SRC-013","SRC-014","SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018","SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-032","SRC-033","SRC-034","SRC-035","SRC-036"],"review_text":"The paper is well-structured, moving logically from the introduction of expressivity measures to theoretical proofs and finally to empirical validation. The terminology is precise, with clear definitions for key concepts such as 'transitions,' 'activation patterns,' and 'dichotomies.' The narrative is smooth, and the connection between the theoretical results and their practical implications for trained networks is well-articulated. The use of a summary table (Table 1) to list key results and their locations is a helpful organizational feature that aids the reader in navigating the paper's contributions.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-011","SRC-012","SRC-013","SRC-014","SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018","SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-032","SRC-033","SRC-034","SRC-035","SRC-036"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined. The paper clearly defines the network architecture, the non-linearities, and the random initialization scheme. The definitions of the three expressivity measures are precise. However, the presentation of Theorem 1 could be improved. The bound is given as E[l(z^(d)(t))] >= O((...)^d) l(x(t)). The use of the Big-O notation on the right-hand side of an inequality is unconventional and potentially confusing, as Big-O typically describes an upper bound on the growth rate of a function, not a lower bound on an expectation. It would be clearer to state the bound with a specific constant or to use Theta notation if the bound is tight in both directions. Additionally, the proof outline in Section 2.2.1 is helpful, but the transition from the recurrence relation to the final bound could be more explicit for a reader who is not familiar with the technical details.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-009","SRC-010","SRC-016","SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-021","SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-032","SRC-033","SRC-034","SRC-035","SRC-036"],"review_text":"The figure captions are detailed and provide sufficient context to understand the visual content. For example, the caption for Figure 1 clearly explains the experimental setup, the variables being plotted, and the relationship between the simulated data and the theoretical bounds. The caption for Figure 3 effectively describes the visualization of input space partitioning into convex polytopes. The Markdown table (Table 1) is readable and serves as a useful summary of the paper's key results. The figure references in the text are consistent and help guide the reader to the relevant visual evidence.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"e629e4802b3de84b6b6ce8f7b5a8a30841ed42a75627f45d3adb950902300f52","paper_id":"B1TTpYKgx","paper_ordinal":11,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"635344269ef0d5f7590a240f32d2044d9e043367db3cc96bac9d61ce252e788f","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1TTpYKgx","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"18b66c2f16767beee95023bc4fb64668b692bb2bc6b0bed7c2a4b24f2cf90145","request_identity_sha256":"befe15cfc81dc8a911a5a3d18af51141ce8f2c6e077e2034e4cdd20b1b4c0057","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":1373,"prompt_tokens":16586,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":17959},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"befe15cfc81dc8a911a5a3d18af51141ce8f2c6e077e2034e4cdd20b1b4c0057","role":"CLAR","role_ordinal":1,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}